  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1223 AM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nBy Sunday evening we could see a lull and decrease in rain across \nour northern and eastern areas including the Austin metro before we \nsee another round of rain form over the Rio Grande and Southern \nEdwards Plateau areas. This 2nd round should continue pushing \neastward late Sunday evening and continuing through the overnight \nhours into Monday morning. Latest global model ensembles now have \nthis batch of rain sticking around through the day Monday and not \nclearing until Monday evening. As previously mentioned we could see \nsome heavier embedded cells in this batch of rain that would be \ncapable of producing heavier rainfall rates across locations that \nare already saturated with earlier rains during the event. WPC \nhighlights a level 1 to 2 risk for flooding across the vast majority \nof our region from Sunday into Monday. As for amounts, we should see \nfairly widespread totals in the 1 to 3 inch range with some isolated \npockets of up to 5 inches not out of the question for areas that see \nrepeated rounds of rainfall. However, almost everyone should see at \nleast a half inch to an inch when all is said and done. These totals \nmay seem like a lot but we arent expecting any heavy torrential \ndownpours but rather some good old fashioned steady cool rain that \nwill occur over a period of several days rather than all at once.\n\nAs far as highs go, with the steady rainfall and extensive cloud \ncover we may see some areas struggle to break out of the mid 50s for \nhighs with most remaining in the low to mid 60s producing yet \nanother dreary and raw day for Monday across our forecast area. Lows \nhowever wont drop off too much as the clouds should keep most of the \narea fairly insulated and prevent any radiational cooling from \nhappening with most staying in the upper 40s to near 50 degrees. \nBeyond Monday as we finally begin to dry out we should see highs \nrebound back near 70 for Tuesday with temps well into the 70s to \nround out the end of the week along with lows remaining in the\n50s.",
